P_review='Review the latest commit (git show HEAD) by reading the diff and the surrounding code. Do not run tests, builds or linters. Report only real defects introduced by this commit. Write your findings as a JSON array to review.json in the repository root, each item {"file": "...", "function": "...", "line": N, "problem": "..."}, and also print them.'
P_debug='Two user reports about codex-router: (1) after a repeated tool failure the router escalates as expected, but the hold after the escalation ends one turn earlier than policy.escalationHoldTurns says; (2) after a long, well-cached session, the switch tax the panel shows is far smaller than the thread size, so the router leaves a warm model too easily. Find the root causes, fix them in non-test code, add regression tests, run go test ./internal/... and report.'
P_ops='CI fails on this branch. The command `make vet release-build` must succeed. Find and fix every cause without weakening the checks: keep all four target platforms (darwin and linux, amd64 and arm64), do not skip packages or delete source files. Report what was wrong.'
P_code='Add support for the "max" reasoning effort to codex-router configuration: routes and activity routes may use effort "max", which is stronger than "xhigh" everywhere efforts are ordered; unknown efforts must still be rejected. Update docs/configuration.md and add tests. Run go test ./internal/... and report.'
P_explore='Answer these questions about this repository (codex-router) by reading its code; do not change files. Write the answers as a JSON object to explore.json in the repository root with exactly these keys and types, then print it: q1_votes_kept (int: how many recent classifier votes the policy keeps); q2_failures_before_pause (int: consecutive classifier failures before it pauses) and q2_pause_seconds (int: pause length); q3_upgrade_bar (number: the upgrade bar with the default balanced policy when the switch tax is exactly 100000 tokens); q4_thrifty_upgradeVotes and q4_thrifty_minDwellRequests (ints under the thrifty preset); q5_reason (string: the Reason policy.Decide returns when the classifier choice is not a known tier) and q5_vote_recorded (bool: is a vote recorded in that case); q6_tax_when_current_cold (int: what Ledger.SwitchTax returns when the thread current model is cold or unknown); q7_health_path (string: the proxy health check path); q8_reason (string: the decision reason when the route model is in another compatibility group than the request model); q9_top_tier_escalates (bool: does a repeated failure escalate when the incumbent is already the top tier with default escalation); q10_strip_cells (int: how many cells the per-session route strip keeps); q11_warm_seconds (int: how long after its last response a model counts as warm with the default cache config); q12_env_var (string: the env var the launcher sets for Codex and the hook with the session control socket).'
P_plan='Write an implementation plan (no code changes) for making codex-router price the model switch tax in US dollars instead of uncached tokens. Read internal/policy, internal/cost, internal/route, internal/config and docs/configuration.md first. Cover design, config changes, edge cases, migration and tests. Write the plan to plan.md in the repository root and print it.'
